p:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Maryland Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession: What Owners Should Know</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Maryland</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Maryland Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Maryland Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession sale</li><li>Turn the Maryland Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Maryland House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Maryland law sets out when a person occupying land can claim title by adverse possession, and how an owner can remove someone who has no right to be there.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Within 20 years from the date the cause of action accrues, a person must file an action for recovery of possession of a corporeal freehold or leasehold estate in land. (Md. Code, Courts &amp; Judicial Proceedings \u00a7 5-103(a)(1); <a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=gcj&section=5-103&enactments=false' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Before an eviction, the landlord must get a judgment in a rent court / breach of lease / holding over case and then petition for a Warrant of Restitution; the sheriff or constable must be present at the eviction, and it cannot occur on a Sunday or holiday. (Housing Cases (Maryland Courts); <a href='https://www.mdcourts.gov/legalhelp/housing' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Maryland?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Maryland houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><h2>Maryland Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession FAQ</h2><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Can a squatter take ownership of my Maryland house?</h3><p> Check the statute and talk to a Maryland attorney about your facts.</p><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/maryland-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Maryland Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/maryland-eviction-notice/'>Maryland Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/maryland-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Maryland guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-maryland/'>We buy houses in Maryland</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=gcj&section=5-103&enactments=false' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Md. Code, Courts &amp; Judicial Proceedings \u00a7 5-103(a)(1)</a></li><li><a href='https://www.mdcourts.gov/legalhelp/housing' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Housing Cases (Maryland Courts)</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Maryland Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can a squatter take ownership of my Maryland house?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Only by meeting every requirement of the adverse possession statute cited above for the full period. Check the statute and talk to a Maryland attorney about your facts.\"}}]}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Maryland\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-maryland/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Maryland Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/maryland-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Maryland Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession", "rank_math_description": "Maryland squatters rights and adverse possession: what the statutes say and how owners remove occupants or sell. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "maryland squatters rights"}, {"slug": "maryland-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights", "title": "Maryland Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: Rules for Selling a Rental", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Maryland Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: Rules for Selling a Rental</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Maryland</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Maryland Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Maryland Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights sale</li><li>Turn the Maryland Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Maryland House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Maryland statutes set the basic rules between landlords and tenants, including deposits, notices and what happens when a rental is sold.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>A landlord may not impose a security deposit in excess of the equivalent of 1 month&#x27;s rent per dwelling unit, regardless of the number of tenants; a landlord who overcharges is liable for up to three times the extra amount plus attorney&#x27;s fees. (Md. Code, Real Property \u00a7 8-203(b)(1), (b)(3); <a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-203&enactments=false' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Within 45 days after the tenancy ends, the landlord must return the deposit with simple interest (greater of the daily U.S. Treasury yield curve rate for 1 year or 1.5% a year), less damages rightfully withheld. (Real Property \u00a7 8-203(e)(1); <a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-203&enactments=false' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>If any deposit is withheld, the landlord must mail an itemized list of damages and costs within 45 days after the tenancy ends or forfeits the right to withhold for damages; wrongful failure to return can cost up to threefold plus attorney&#x27;s fees. (Real Property \u00a7 8-203(e)(4), (g); <a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-203&enactments=false' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>For a written lease for a term over 1 week or a month-to-month tenancy, notice to terminate is 60 days before expiration of the tenancy; year-to-year is 90 days; week-to-week is 7 days (written lease) or 21 days (no written lease). (Real Property \u00a7 8-402(b)-(c); <a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-402' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A tenant may use rent escrow (paying rent to a third party/court) where the landlord fails to fix defects after notice; the tenant must first notify the landlord of defects and request repairs. (Housing Cases (Maryland Courts); <a href='https://www.mdcourts.gov/legalhelp/housing' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Maryland?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Maryland houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/maryland-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>Maryland Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/maryland-eviction-notice/'>Maryland Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/maryland-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Maryland guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-maryland/'>We buy houses in Maryland</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-203&enactments=false' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Md. Code, Real Property \u00a7 8-203(b)(1), (b)(3)</a></li><li><a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-402' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Real Property \u00a7 8-402(b)-(c)</a></li><li><a href='https://www.mdcourts.gov/legalhelp/housing' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Housing Cases (Maryland Courts)</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Maryland Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Maryland\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-maryland/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Maryland Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/maryland-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Maryland Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights", "rank_math_description": "Maryland landlord tenant law and tenant rights: deposits, notices, entry and selling a rented house. Official sources only.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "maryland tenant rights"}, {"slug": "maryland-eviction-notice", "title": "Maryland Eviction Notice Rules: Notice Types, Days and Selling the House", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Maryland Eviction Notice Rules: Notice Types, Days and Selling the House</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Maryland</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Maryland Eviction Notice Rules: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Maryland Eviction Notice Rules sale</li><li>Turn the Maryland Eviction Notice Rules offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Maryland House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Maryland law requires a landlord to give a specific written notice before filing an eviction, and the number of days depends on the reason.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Before filing a failure-to-pay-rent case, landlord must give the tenant written notice of intent to file, giving 10 days to cure, on a Judiciary-created form (DC-CV-115); the complaint must state the date notice was given. (Real Property \u00a7 8-401(c); <a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-401&enactments=false' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Nonpayment cases are filed in the District Court; the judgment orders possession within 4 days after trial (extendable up to 15 days with a physician certificate); if the tenant tenders rent, late fees and costs at trial, the complaint is satisfied. (Real Property \u00a7 8-401; <a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-401&enactments=false' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>If the tenant does not comply within 7 days of a landlord judgment, the court issues a warrant of restitution to a county official, who may remove the tenant&#x27;s goods. (Real Property \u00a7 8-401(f)(1); <a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-401&enactments=false' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Breach of lease: landlord must give 30 days&#x27; written notice that the tenant is in violation and the landlord wants to repossess (one of the alternatives in the section). (Real Property \u00a7 8-402.1; <a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-402.1&enactments=false' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>No-cause/end of term: 60 days&#x27; notice for month-to-month tenancy or a written term lease over 1 week; 90 days for year-to-year. (Real Property \u00a7 8-402; <a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-402' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Landlord must notify tenant of the eviction date at least 6 days before eviction (mail with certificate of mailing, post on property, and send electronically if email/cell known); the sheriff or constable carries out the eviction. (Housing Cases (Maryland Courts); Real Property \u00a7 8-407; <a href='https://www.mdcourts.gov/legalhelp/housing' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Maryland?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Maryland houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/maryland-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>Maryland Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/maryland-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Maryland Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/maryland-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Maryland guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-maryland/'>We buy houses in Maryland</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-401&enactments=false' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Real Property \u00a7 8-401(c)</a></li><li><a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-402.1&enactments=false' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Real Property \u00a7 8-402.1</a></li><li><a href='https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=grp&section=8-402' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Real Property \u00a7 8-402</a></li><li><a href='https://www.mdcourts.gov/legalhelp/housing' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Housing Cases (Maryland Courts); Real Property \u00a7 8-407</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Maryland Eviction Notice Rules, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Maryland\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-maryland/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Maryland Eviction Notice: Types and Days\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/maryland-eviction-notice/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Maryland Eviction Notice: Types and Days", "rank_math_description": "Maryland eviction notice rules: notice types, required days, which court hears the case and selling a rental. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "maryland eviction notice"}]